    "pages":{
        "home": {
            "default": "Home",
            "description": "Hi! I am Federico Mattucci, a Computer Science student at the University of Pisa. With this site I want to tell you a little bit about myself."
        },
        "experience": {
            "default": "Experience",
            "description": "This section is dedicated to my work experiences and internships."
        },
        "portfolio": {
            "default": "Portfolio",
            "description": "Here you can find some of my projects and works.",
            "photography-description": "I got into photography in a completely unexpected way. One day, my father asked me to take pictures of watches he wanted to put up for sale. At the time, I had a phone that did not yet have a well-developed camera and no knowledge of photography. When I started taking pictures, I realized that all the pictures were full of reflections, overexposed or underexposed. Since I had no tools to take well-done photos, I began to engineer myself to be able to \"create\" them. I made \"panels\" to use as softboxes using four sheets of paper on which I had printed pages that were all black. These allowed me to remove reflections, but they also made the photos underexposed. I then also created a light with a diffuser using again white sheets of paper and a light with a spring arm, so as to better illuminate the clocks. At first I didn't like it because it was too complicated, but then as time went on, taking pictures of these objects, I began to get hooked, and from there my study of photography began."
        },
